    brief: ['Seventh Army lands at Licata, Gela and Scoglitti while Eighth Army lands at Pachino, Avola and Cassibile. Get ashore against the coastal divisions, hold the Gela beachhead when the Hermann Goering Division and Livorno counterattack, take the airfields and the port of Syracuse, then drive for Catania and Enna before the Germans seal the Catania plain.', 'The coastal divisions will not hold. Strike the Gela and Scoglitti beachheads with Hermann Goering, Livorno and the mobile groups before the Americans land their tanks and guns, hold Kampfgruppe Schmalz in front of Catania, and fall back fighting to the Simeto line as the paratroops and 15. Panzergrenadier-Division arrive.'],
    hist: 'Historically Syracuse fell on the evening of D-Day. The Gela counterattacks of 10 and 11 July reached the dunes and were broken by infantry, artillery and naval gunfire. Augusta fell on 13 July, the fight for Primosole bridge lasted from 13 to 17 July, and Eighth Army then stalled in front of Catania while Seventh Army took Caltanissetta and Enna.'
